ers in Psychology</em>, 12, 727542. DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2021.727542">10.3389/fpsyg.2021.727542</a></li>\n<li>Price, D. (2021). <em>Laziness Does Not Exist</em>. New York: Atria Books.</li>\n<li>Weir, E., Allison, C., Warrier, V., &amp; Baron-Cohen, S. (2021). Increased prevalence of psychiatric conditions and substance use among autistic individuals: A UK Biobank study. <em>The Lancet Psychiatry</em>, 8(8), 706–718.</li>\n<li>Belcher, H. L., Morein-Zamir, S., Mandy, W., &amp; Ford, R. M. (2022). Camouflaging Intent, First Impressions, and Age of ASC Diagnosis in Autistic Men and Women. <em>Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders</em>, 52(8), 3413–3426.<br>DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-021-05221-3">10.1007/s10803-021-05221-3</a><br>PubMed: <a class="link" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34342806/">https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34342806/</a><br>PMC: <a class="link" href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9296412/">https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9296412/</a></li>\n<li>Harris, S. S., Green, S. M., Kumar, M., &amp; Urs, N. M. (2022). A role for cortical dopamine in the paradoxical calming effects of psychostimulants. <em>Scientific Reports</em>, 12, 3129. DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-07029-2">10.1038/s41598-022-07029-2</a>. PMC: <a class="link" href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8873208/">https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8873208/</a></li>\n<li>Milton, D., Gurbuz, E., &amp; López, B. (2022). The ''double empathy problem'': Ten years on. <em>Autism</em>, 26(8), 1901–1903. DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1177/13623613221129123">10.1177/13623613221129123</a></li>\n<li>Chapman, R., &amp; Botha, M. (2023). Neurodivergence-informed therapy. <em>Developmental Medicine &amp; Child Neurology</em>, 65(3), 310–317.<br>DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1111/dmcn.15384">10.1111/dmcn.15384</a></li>\n<li>Wilson, R. B., et al. (2023). Autistic women''s experiences of self-compassion after receiving their diagnosis in adulthood. <em>Autism</em>, 27(7), 1336–1347. DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1177/13623613221136752">10.1177/13623613221136752</a></li>\n<li>Neff, M. A. (2024). <em>Self-Care for Autistic People: 100+ Ways to Recharge, De-Stress, and Unmask!</em> Avon, MA: Adams Media (Simon &amp; Schuster).</li>\n<li>Holborn, T., Schifano, F., Smith, E., &amp; Deluca, P. (2025). The Use of Novel Stimulants in ADHD Self-Medication. <em>Brain Sciences</em>, 15(3), 292. DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.3390/brainsci15030292">10.3390/brainsci15030292</a></li>\n</ol>\n\n<hr class="separator">','\n',char(10)),'The 15 most important for this body of work','A selection for a person with AuDHD in a corporate environment: camouflaging, open loops, double empathy, monotropism, self-medication, risk, and the direct overlap of ASD and ADHD in adulthood. The original TOP 10 was retained; five new items were added from Appendix 1.',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO content_sections VALUES(853,30,850,'heading',2,2,4,'Appendix 1 — ASD ↔ ADHD / AuDHD: uzupełnienie','appendix-1-asd-adhd-audhd-uzupelnienie','20 nowych artykułów dodanych 2026-08-26: 7 pozycji wyprowadzonych z bibliografii/cytowań artykułu Centrum Aura oraz 13 pozycji dobranych dodatkowo pod zidentyfikowane luki: bezpośredni fenotyp ASD+ADHD, przebieg przez życie, rodziny i genetyka, funkcjonowanie…',4,replace('<p class="podtytul">20 nowych artykułów dodanych 2026-08-26: 7 pozycji wyprowadzonych z bibliografii/cytowań artykułu Centrum Aura oraz 13 pozycji dobranych dodatkowo pod zidentyfikowane luki: bezpośredni fenotyp ASD+ADHD, przebieg przez życie, rodziny i genetyka, funkcjonowanie dorosłych, diagnostyka różnicowa i maskowanie. Pozycje nie dublują listy głównej 77.</p>\n\n<ol class="lista-publikacji">\n<li>Reiersen, A. M., Constantino, J. N., Grimmer, M., Martin, N. G., &amp; Todd, R. D. (2008). Evidence for shared genetic influences on self-reported ADHD and autistic symptoms in young adult Australian twins. <em>Twin Research and Human Genetics</em>, 11(6), 579–585.<br>DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1375/twin.11.6.579">10.1375/twin.11.6.579</a><br>PubMed: <a class="link" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19016613/">https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19016613/</a><br>PMC: <a class="link" href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2840992/">https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2840992/</a></li>\n<li>Ronald, A., Simonoff, E., Kuntsi, J., Asherson, P., &amp; Plomin, R. (2008). Evidence for overlapping genetic influences on autistic and ADHD behaviours in a community twin sample. <em>Journal of Child Psychology and Psychiatry</em>, 49(5), 535–542.<br>DOI: <a class="link" href="https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7610.2007.01857.x">10.1111/j.1469-7610.2007.01857.x</a><br>PubMed: <a class="link" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18221348/">https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18221348/</a></li>\n<li>Szaniawska, M. (2010). Trudna diagnoza –